
		     Directions for running the

		   PROGRAMMABLE LOGIC USER'S GUIDE


 The  User's  Guide  is distributed on IBM (tm) PC-DOS Double-Sided 2.0
 Format   disks  (9 Sectors per track). You must run under DOS	2.0  or
 later to use the disk. Also, the User's Guide runs on the IBM PC or an
 equivalent such as the Compaq, Columbia, Eagle, etc.

 Be sure to make backup copies of the disk before using.

 To run the Programmable Logic User's Guide simply type:

			       PLUG

 and then press the <enter> key.



